<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The decision playbook | BTCisGTO</title><meta name="description" content="A practical framework for learning, testing decisions, building useful tools, and working toward Lola’s HOME."><link rel="canonical" href="https://btcisgto.cloud/playbook/"><meta property="og:title" content="The decision playbook | BTCisGTO"><meta property="og:description" content="A practical framework for learning, testing decisions, building useful tools, and working toward Lola’s HOME."><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:url" content="https://btcisgto.cloud/playbook/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/mission-v1.css"><script src="/assets/mission-v1.js" defer></script></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><div class="shell header-inner"><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="BTCisGTO home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">₿</span>BTC<span>is</span>GTO</a><button class="menu-button" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-expanded="false">Menu</button><nav class="nav" id="main-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/tools/" >Tools</a><a href="/goal/" >The mission</a><a href="/treasury/" >Treasury</a><a href="/building/" >Build log</a><a href="/learn/" aria-current="page">Learn</a></nav><a class="btn primary header-cta" href="/tradingtool/">Start practicing ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="shell"><div class="page-head"><div class="eyebrow">The playbook</div><h1>Think in probabilities.<br><em>Build with purpose.</em></h1><p>GTO means game theory optimal. Here it inspires a disciplined approach to decisions; it is not proof that Bitcoin, a trading strategy, or a life plan must succeed.</p></div></div><div class="shell"><article class="prose"><h2>Six moves for the long game</h2><h3>01 · Understand the game</h3><p>Write down the rules, incentives, costs, and uncertainties. Separate what you know from what you assume. Read original sources when they are available.</p><h3>02 · Practice before committing capital</h3><p>Use the Trading Sim to learn order behavior, sizing, and journaling. Simulated performance is a learning record, not evidence of future real-money returns.</p><h3>03 · Forecast before seeing the price</h3><p>Use Edge to record your own probability range and the resolution criteria. Then compare the forecast with executable prices, costs, and uncertainty. Passing is a valid outcome.</p><h3>04 · Review the result honestly</h3><p>Keep losing decisions and passes in the record. Ask whether the process was sound, not simply whether a single outcome went your way.</p><h3>05 · Build useful work into a business</h3><p>Serve a narrow audience well. Verify revenue and expenses before allocating profit. Agents, automation, and the Hydra Protocol remain research directions until performance and controls are demonstrated.</p><h3>06 · Connect the work to the mission</h3><p>Work toward Lola’s HOME through documented milestones. A place built on care deserves the same rigor as the tools intended to help fund it.</p><div class="note">Earlier architecture ideas included Lightning routing, staking, and funding-rate strategies. These are not active product offers, verified yields, or instructions to deploy capital.</div><div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/tradingtool/">Practice in the Trading Sim <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="btn " href="/edge/">Research with Edge <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="shell"><div class="footer-top"><div><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="BTCisGTO home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">₿</span>BTC<span>is</span>GTO</a><p>Bitcoin. Truth. Compassion.<br>Useful tools. A public journey.<br>A long road toward Lola’s HOME.</p></div><div class="footer-links"><div><strong>Use</strong><a href="/tradin